{"id":"forecast-03","section":4,"path":"bank/listening/forecast-03/audio-4.mp3","model":"small","duration":1064.09,"segments":[{"start":0.0,"end":5.5,"text":"Part 4 You will hear a zoology lecturer talking about","words":[["Part",0.0,0.54],["4",0.54,1.02],["You",1.02,2.52],["will",2.52,2.74],["hear",2.74,3.0],["a",3.0,3.22],["zoology",3.22,3.76],["lecturer",3.76,4.22],["talking",4.22,5.12],["about",5.12,5.5]]},{"start":5.5,"end":13.22,"text":"a group of primitive animals called gastropods. First you have some time to look at questions","words":[["a",5.5,5.76],["group",5.76,5.98],["of",5.98,6.26],["primitive",6.26,6.62],["animals",6.62,7.38],["called",7.38,7.98],["gastropods.",7.98,9.28],["First",10.52,11.24],["you",11.24,11.5],["have",11.5,11.68],["some",11.68,11.88],["time",11.88,12.28],["to",12.28,12.58],["look",12.58,12.72],["at",12.72,12.86],["questions",12.86,13.22]]},{"start":13.22,"end":69.68,"text":"31 to 40. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.","words":[["31",13.22,14.04],["to",14.04,14.3],["40.",14.3,14.72],["Now",65.7,66.06],["listen",66.06,66.44],["carefully",66.44,66.94],["and",66.94,67.3],["answer",67.3,67.72],["questions",67.72,68.2],["31",68.2,69.02],["to",69.02,69.28],["40.",69.28,69.68]]},{"start":72.68,"end":77.78,"text":"Good morning everyone. In this module we've been looking at various field survey methods","words":[["Good",72.68,73.36],["morning",73.36,73.64],["everyone.",73.64,74.0],["In",74.62,74.92],["this",74.92,75.1],["module",75.1,75.46],["we've",75.46,75.76],["been",75.76,75.88],["looking",75.88,76.08],["at",76.08,76.3],["various",76.3,76.66],["field",76.66,77.02],["survey",77.02,77.42],["methods",77.42,77.78]]},{"start":78.24,"end":82.84,"text":"and now I'm going to give you a brief introduction to the specific organism that will be","words":[["and",78.24,78.6],["now",78.6,78.84],["I'm",78.84,79.12],["going",79.12,79.28],["to",79.28,79.46],["give",79.46,79.64],["you",79.64,79.76],["a",79.76,79.9],["brief",79.9,80.06],["introduction",80.06,80.7],["to",80.7,81.02],["the",81.02,81.12],["specific",81.12,81.5],["organism",81.5,82.1],["that",82.1,82.58],["will",82.58,82.7],["be",82.7,82.84]]},{"start":82.84,"end":89.96,"text":"focusing on during our first field trip, and that's the gastropod. Gastropods are invertebrates,","words":[["focusing",82.84,83.2],["on",83.2,83.52],["during",83.52,83.74],["our",83.74,83.98],["first",83.98,84.32],["field",84.32,84.68],["trip,",84.68,84.98],["and",85.48,85.78],["that's",85.78,86.16],["the",86.16,86.28],["gastropod.",86.28,87.0],["Gastropods",88.12,88.76],["are",88.76,89.1],["invertebrates,",89.1,89.96]]},{"start":90.5,"end":96.14,"text":"their organisms without a backbone, and they're more commonly known as snails or, if they","words":[["their",90.5,90.62],["organisms",90.62,91.12],["without",91.12,91.58],["a",91.58,91.88],["backbone,",91.88,92.36],["and",92.92,93.16],["they're",93.16,93.34],["more",93.34,93.48],["commonly",93.48,93.9],["known",93.9,94.24],["as",94.24,94.62],["snails",94.62,95.22],["or,",95.22,95.54],["if",95.68,95.98],["they",95.98,96.14]]},{"start":96.14,"end":103.02,"text":"haven't got a shell, slugs. Now, in terms of their evolution, gastropods go back a","words":[["haven't",96.14,96.42],["got",96.42,96.58],["a",96.58,96.76],["shell,",96.76,97.02],["slugs.",97.52,97.88],["Now,",98.96,99.2],["in",99.66,99.88],["terms",99.88,100.16],["of",100.16,100.46],["their",100.46,100.64],["evolution,",100.64,101.24],["gastropods",101.76,102.38],["go",102.38,102.62],["back",102.62,102.86],["a",102.86,103.02]]},{"start":103.02,"end":108.54,"text":"long way. As with other primitive animals, the minerals in their body fluids are very","words":[["long",103.02,103.24],["way.",103.24,103.6],["As",104.1,104.4],["with",104.4,104.62],["other",104.62,104.88],["primitive",104.88,105.22],["animals,",105.22,105.72],["the",106.18,106.34],["minerals",106.34,106.66],["in",106.66,106.98],["their",106.98,107.14],["body",107.14,107.38],["fluids",107.38,107.76],["are",107.76,108.3],["very",108.3,108.54]]},{"start":108.54,"end":114.54,"text":"similar to the mineral composition of the sea, indicating that they began life there. And","words":[["similar",108.54,108.96],["to",108.96,109.16],["the",109.16,109.28],["mineral",109.28,109.54],["composition",109.54,110.06],["of",110.06,110.38],["the",110.38,110.5],["sea,",110.5,110.88],["indicating",111.24,111.68],["that",111.68,112.22],["they",112.22,112.34],["began",112.34,112.72],["life",112.72,113.06],["there.",113.06,113.46],["And",114.26,114.54]]},{"start":114.54,"end":120.28,"text":"their fossilised remains have been found in rocks dating back at least 500 million years.","words":[["their",114.54,114.7],["fossilised",114.7,115.42],["remains",115.42,115.78],["have",115.78,116.22],["been",116.22,116.38],["found",116.38,116.68],["in",116.68,116.9],["rocks",116.9,117.24],["dating",117.24,117.58],["back",117.58,117.92],["at",117.92,118.1],["least",118.1,118.38],["500",118.38,118.98],["million",118.98,119.74],["years.",119.74,120.28]]},{"start":121.54,"end":127.56,"text":"Looking at the physical features of the gastropods, well, they all have one muscular foot for","words":[["Looking",121.54,121.98],["at",121.98,122.24],["the",122.24,122.34],["physical",122.34,122.74],["features",122.74,123.2],["of",123.2,123.4],["the",123.4,123.5],["gastropods,",123.5,124.12],["well,",124.66,124.98],["they",125.32,125.44],["all",125.44,125.66],["have",125.66,125.9],["one",125.9,126.16],["muscular",126.16,126.74],["foot",126.74,127.16],["for",127.16,127.56]]},{"start":127.56,"end":133.4,"text":"swimming or walking. This foot is lubricated with mucus, and it's this that leaves the","words":[["swimming",127.56,127.86],["or",127.86,128.22],["walking.",128.22,128.62],["This",129.36,129.7],["foot",129.7,129.96],["is",129.96,130.22],["lubricated",130.22,130.92],["with",130.92,131.18],["mucus,",131.18,131.66],["and",132.08,132.3],["it's",132.3,132.5],["this",132.5,132.72],["that",132.72,132.96],["leaves",132.96,133.2],["the",133.2,133.4]]},{"start":133.4,"end":139.24,"text":"sticky trail that you see behind snails and slugs. They also have an organ called a","words":[["sticky",133.4,133.72],["trail",133.72,134.12],["that",134.12,134.38],["you",134.38,134.48],["see",134.48,134.72],["behind",134.72,135.26],["snails",135.26,135.8],["and",135.8,135.96],["slugs.",135.96,136.38],["They",137.28,137.54],["also",137.54,137.82],["have",137.82,138.06],["an",138.06,138.2],["organ",138.2,138.42],["called",138.42,138.96],["a",138.96,139.24]]},{"start":139.24,"end":145.2,"text":"radula, which they use for feeding. Then of course the snails, though not the","words":[["radula,",139.24,139.8],["which",140.16,140.46],["they",140.46,140.66],["use",140.66,140.92],["for",140.92,141.12],["feeding.",141.12,141.46],["Then",142.48,142.7],["of",142.7,142.86],["course",142.86,143.12],["the",143.12,143.52],["snails,",143.52,144.1],["though",144.3,144.64],["not",144.64,145.02],["the",145.02,145.2]]},{"start":145.2,"end":151.54,"text":"slugs, have a shell. In terms of their dimensions, snail shells in Britain range","words":[["slugs,",145.2,145.7],["have",145.98,146.16],["a",146.16,146.44],["shell.",146.44,146.7],["In",147.7,147.98],["terms",147.98,148.22],["of",148.22,148.46],["their",148.46,148.58],["dimensions,",148.58,149.32],["snail",149.86,150.14],["shells",150.14,150.4],["in",150.4,150.68],["Britain",150.68,150.98],["range",150.98,151.54]]},{"start":151.54,"end":156.86,"text":"from the dwarf snail, which is 1.5 millimeters long, to the Roman snail,","words":[["from",151.54,151.78],["the",151.78,151.94],["dwarf",151.94,152.2],["snail,",152.2,152.58],["which",153.02,153.3],["is",153.3,153.44],["1",153.44,153.7],[".5",153.7,154.38],["millimeters",154.38,154.78],["long,",154.78,155.32],["to",155.62,155.94],["the",155.94,156.08],["Roman",156.08,156.42],["snail,",156.42,156.86]]},{"start":157.26,"end":162.38,"text":"whose shell can be as big as 50 millimeters. As well as size variations,","words":[["whose",157.26,157.48],["shell",157.48,157.78],["can",157.78,157.98],["be",157.98,158.14],["as",158.14,158.28],["big",158.28,158.52],["as",158.52,158.78],["50",158.78,159.24],["millimeters.",159.24,159.66],["As",160.72,161.28],["well",161.28,161.48],["as",161.48,161.64],["size",161.64,161.94],["variations,",161.94,162.38]]},{"start":162.38,"end":168.14,"text":"variations, you get a lot of differences in the form of snail shells. For example, the","words":[["variations,",162.38,162.7],["you",163.12,163.34],["get",163.34,163.58],["a",163.58,163.78],["lot",163.78,163.94],["of",163.94,164.08],["differences",164.08,164.54],["in",164.54,164.94],["the",164.94,165.08],["form",165.08,165.42],["of",165.42,165.62],["snail",165.62,165.88],["shells.",165.88,166.22],["For",166.9,167.1],["example,",167.1,167.44],["the",168.0,168.14]]},{"start":168.14,"end":173.82,"text":"majority coil to the right, but there are a few that coil to the left. Then some shells,","words":[["majority",168.14,168.56],["coil",168.56,169.12],["to",169.12,169.36],["the",169.36,169.48],["right,",169.48,169.84],["but",170.2,170.34],["there",170.34,170.48],["are",170.48,170.6],["a",170.6,170.78],["few",170.78,171.0],["that",171.0,171.2],["coil",171.2,171.5],["to",171.5,171.68],["the",171.68,171.8],["left.",171.8,172.2],["Then",172.68,172.98],["some",172.98,173.4],["shells,",173.4,173.82]]},{"start":174.24,"end":180.74,"text":"for instance, the plated snail, have regularly spaced ribs, while the prickly snail has","words":[["for",174.24,174.4],["instance,",174.4,174.7],["the",175.22,175.36],["plated",175.36,175.74],["snail,",175.74,176.1],["have",176.58,176.84],["regularly",176.84,177.48],["spaced",177.48,177.96],["ribs,",177.96,178.5],["while",178.94,179.32],["the",179.32,179.5],["prickly",179.5,179.88],["snail",179.88,180.24],["has",180.24,180.74]]},{"start":180.74,"end":187.34,"text":"prominent spines. There are even a number of species with hair on their shells. Colours","words":[["prominent",180.74,181.2],["spines.",181.2,181.92],["There",182.76,183.26],["are",183.26,183.42],["even",183.42,183.66],["a",183.66,183.82],["number",183.82,184.02],["of",184.02,184.18],["species",184.18,184.54],["with",184.54,184.94],["hair",184.94,185.22],["on",185.22,185.38],["their",185.38,185.58],["shells.",185.58,185.92],["Colours",186.84,187.34]]},{"start":187.34,"end":192.7,"text":"on the shells also vary as do patterns, so appearances are really varied.","words":[["on",187.34,187.5],["the",187.5,187.68],["shells",187.68,188.02],["also",188.02,188.54],["vary",188.54,188.96],["as",188.96,189.28],["do",189.28,189.48],["patterns,",189.48,189.9],["so",190.46,190.72],["appearances",190.72,191.22],["are",191.22,191.76],["really",191.76,192.22],["varied.",192.22,192.7]]},{"start":197.92,"end":204.0,"text":"Okay, let's turn now to feeding habits. Most of you who are gardeners will know to","words":[["Okay,",197.92,198.28],["let's",198.9,199.26],["turn",199.26,199.46],["now",199.46,199.76],["to",199.76,200.0],["feeding",200.0,200.46],["habits.",200.46,200.96],["Most",201.78,202.0],["of",202.0,202.16],["you",202.16,202.34],["who",202.34,202.48],["are",202.48,202.6],["gardeners",202.6,203.16],["will",203.16,203.54],["know",203.54,203.76],["to",203.76,204.0]]},{"start":204.0,"end":209.96,"text":"your cost that some gastropods eat healthy plants. But you may not realise that these","words":[["your",204.0,204.22],["cost",204.22,204.72],["that",204.72,205.22],["some",205.22,205.5],["gastropods",205.5,206.22],["eat",206.22,206.52],["healthy",206.52,207.0],["plants.",207.0,207.52],["But",208.08,208.48],["you",208.48,208.66],["may",208.66,208.78],["not",208.78,208.96],["realise",208.96,209.28],["that",209.28,209.74],["these",209.74,209.96]]},{"start":209.96,"end":220.6,"text":"are the minority. Most species feed on rotting plants, or they eat fungi and algae. Some","words":[["are",209.96,210.28],["the",210.28,210.42],["minority.",210.42,211.06],["Most",211.98,212.3],["species",212.3,212.64],["feed",212.64,213.26],["on",213.26,213.48],["rotting",213.48,214.0],["plants,",214.0,214.4],["or",214.84,215.18],["they",215.18,215.38],["eat",215.38,215.58],["fungi",215.58,215.94],["and",215.94,216.4],["algae.",216.4,216.74],["Some",220.4,220.6]]},{"start":220.6,"end":226.52,"text":"are some that are actually carnivorous. They prey on live animals. For example, the shield","words":[["are",220.6,220.74],["some",220.74,220.96],["that",220.96,221.16],["are",221.16,221.32],["actually",221.32,221.66],["carnivorous.",221.66,222.48],["They",222.88,222.98],["prey",222.98,223.26],["on",223.26,223.5],["live",223.5,223.76],["animals.",223.76,224.12],["For",225.02,225.24],["example,",225.24,225.6],["the",226.12,226.2],["shield",226.2,226.52]]},{"start":226.52,"end":232.24,"text":"slug feuds on worms. And apart from their own feeding habits, I should point out that","words":[["slug",226.52,226.92],["feuds",226.92,227.26],["on",227.26,227.44],["worms.",227.44,227.78],["And",228.84,229.14],["apart",229.14,229.42],["from",229.42,229.64],["their",229.64,229.82],["own",229.82,230.1],["feeding",230.1,230.44],["habits,",230.44,230.86],["I",231.26,231.42],["should",231.42,231.6],["point",231.6,231.88],["out",231.88,232.1],["that",232.1,232.24]]},{"start":232.24,"end":239.84,"text":"gastropods themselves have plenty of predators. Birds and frogs are the main ones. But there's","words":[["gastropods",232.24,232.92],["themselves",232.92,233.36],["have",233.36,233.86],["plenty",233.86,234.38],["of",234.38,234.6],["predators.",234.6,234.9],["Birds",236.06,236.36],["and",236.36,236.84],["frogs",236.84,237.24],["are",237.24,237.6],["the",237.6,237.68],["main",237.68,237.92],["ones.",237.92,238.24],["But",238.88,239.42],["there's",239.42,239.84]]},{"start":239.84,"end":244.3,"text":"even an entire family of flies that have specialised in preying on gastropods.","words":[["even",239.84,240.16],["an",240.16,240.32],["entire",240.32,240.76],["family",240.76,241.26],["of",241.26,241.46],["flies",241.46,241.8],["that",241.8,242.04],["have",242.04,242.14],["specialised",242.14,242.9],["in",242.9,243.02],["preying",243.02,243.48],["on",243.48,243.6],["gastropods.",243.6,244.3]]},{"start":245.14,"end":250.3,"text":"And of course, last but not least, I should mention human predators.","words":[["And",245.14,245.82],["of",245.82,246.02],["course,",246.02,246.32],["last",246.54,246.94],["but",246.94,247.3],["not",247.3,247.5],["least,",247.5,247.84],["I",248.32,248.46],["should",248.46,248.72],["mention",248.72,249.14],["human",249.14,249.86],["predators.",249.86,250.3]]},{"start":251.48,"end":256.46,"text":"It was the Romans who probably first introduced edible snails into Britain during the first","words":[["It",251.48,251.72],["was",251.72,251.84],["the",251.84,251.98],["Romans",251.98,252.24],["who",252.24,252.56],["probably",252.56,252.98],["first",252.98,253.34],["introduced",253.34,253.9],["edible",253.9,254.32],["snails",254.32,254.9],["into",254.9,255.14],["Britain",255.14,255.44],["during",255.44,255.9],["the",255.9,256.14],["first",256.14,256.46]]},{"start":256.46,"end":259.04,"text":"century and they are still eaten today.","words":[["century",256.46,257.06],["and",257.06,257.66],["they",257.66,257.8],["are",257.8,257.9],["still",257.9,258.18],["eaten",258.18,258.6],["today.",258.6,259.04]]},{"start":259.94,"end":265.38,"text":"In fact, the collection of wild snails for cooking has caused local extinctions of","words":[["In",259.94,260.12],["fact,",260.12,260.44],["the",260.82,260.88],["collection",260.88,261.28],["of",261.28,261.52],["wild",261.52,261.8],["snails",261.8,262.3],["for",262.3,262.48],["cooking",262.48,262.8],["has",262.8,263.46],["caused",263.46,263.88],["local",263.88,264.34],["extinctions",264.34,265.08],["of",265.08,265.38]]},{"start":265.38,"end":268.62,"text":"one species, which is also under threat internationally.","words":[["one",265.38,265.6],["species,",265.6,266.02],["which",266.5,266.76],["is",266.76,266.92],["also",266.92,267.24],["under",267.24,267.52],["threat",267.52,267.9],["internationally.",267.9,268.62]]},{"start":268.62,"end":275.36,"text":"So, there are lots of predators, but to protect themselves, gastropods have often developed","words":[["So,",268.62,269.78],["there",270.02,270.2],["are",270.2,270.3],["lots",270.3,270.64],["of",270.64,270.88],["predators,",270.88,271.2],["but",271.86,272.14],["to",272.14,272.28],["protect",272.28,272.58],["themselves,",272.58,273.12],["gastropods",273.68,274.28],["have",274.28,274.56],["often",274.56,274.9],["developed",274.9,275.36]]},{"start":275.36,"end":276.68,"text":"special defences.","words":[["special",275.36,275.92],["defences.",275.92,276.68]]},{"start":277.34,"end":278.84,"text":"I'll just give you one example.","words":[["I'll",277.34,277.66],["just",277.66,277.82],["give",277.82,278.0],["you",278.0,278.18],["one",278.18,278.42],["example.",278.42,278.84]]},{"start":279.8,"end":285.9,"text":"The glutinous snail avoids predators by folding its mantle over its shell and turning itself","words":[["The",279.8,279.92],["glutinous",279.92,280.52],["snail",280.52,280.78],["avoids",280.78,281.34],["predators",281.34,281.84],["by",281.84,282.18],["folding",282.18,282.6],["its",282.6,282.84],["mantle",282.84,283.26],["over",283.26,283.96],["its",283.96,284.18],["shell",284.18,284.54],["and",284.54,285.12],["turning",285.12,285.44],["itself",285.44,285.9]]},{"start":285.9,"end":288.36,"text":"into a very slippery blob of jelly.","words":[["into",285.9,286.24],["a",286.24,286.42],["very",286.42,286.64],["slippery",286.64,287.2],["blob",287.2,287.76],["of",287.76,288.04],["jelly.",288.04,288.36]]},{"start":289.74,"end":296.48,"text":"Well, turning now to gastropod habitats, most species like dampness and shade.","words":[["Well,",289.74,290.54],["turning",290.8,291.24],["now",291.24,291.58],["to",291.58,291.78],["gastropod",291.78,292.42],["habitats,",292.42,292.98],["most",293.68,294.04],["species",294.04,294.5],["like",294.5,295.02],["dampness",295.02,295.66],["and",295.66,296.06],["shade.",296.06,296.48]]},{"start":296.48,"end":303.82,"text":"In general, both very hot and very cold weather is bad for gastropods, but dry conditions","words":[["In",296.48,297.76],["general,",297.76,298.2],["both",298.7,298.86],["very",298.86,299.28],["hot",299.28,299.74],["and",299.74,300.08],["very",300.08,300.34],["cold",300.34,300.72],["weather",300.72,301.02],["is",301.02,301.34],["bad",301.34,301.68],["for",301.68,301.9],["gastropods,",301.9,302.52],["but",302.84,303.24],["dry",303.24,303.52],["conditions",303.52,303.82]]},{"start":303.82,"end":310.62,"text":"are the least favourable. Snails cope with this by withdrawing into their shells, and","words":[["are",303.82,304.34],["the",304.34,304.48],["least",304.48,304.82],["favourable.",304.82,305.4],["Snails",306.28,306.86],["cope",306.86,307.14],["with",307.14,307.4],["this",307.4,307.58],["by",307.58,308.06],["withdrawing",308.06,308.76],["into",308.76,309.08],["their",309.08,309.32],["shells,",309.32,309.72],["and",310.32,310.62]]},{"start":310.62,"end":315.24,"text":"often they form a thick film of mucus over the mouth of their shell to minimise loss","words":[["often",310.62,310.9],["they",310.9,311.1],["form",311.1,311.38],["a",311.38,311.52],["thick",311.52,311.82],["film",311.82,312.22],["of",312.22,312.38],["mucus",312.38,312.74],["over",312.74,313.1],["the",313.1,313.22],["mouth",313.22,313.5],["of",313.5,313.62],["their",313.62,313.8],["shell",313.8,314.1],["to",314.1,314.48],["minimise",314.48,315.0],["loss",315.0,315.24]]},{"start":315.24,"end":321.98,"text":"of water. Habitats with a long, stable history tend to support the biggest range of gastropod","words":[["of",315.24,315.44],["water.",315.44,315.82],["Habitats",317.0,317.64],["with",317.64,317.82],["a",317.82,317.96],["long,",317.96,318.2],["stable",318.34,318.7],["history",318.7,319.24],["tend",319.24,319.84],["to",319.84,320.06],["support",320.06,320.34],["the",320.34,320.54],["biggest",320.54,320.8],["range",320.8,321.26],["of",321.26,321.44],["gastropod",321.44,321.98]]},{"start":321.98,"end":328.34,"text":"species. So, for instance, long-established forests usually support more species than","words":[["species.",321.98,322.4],["So,",323.14,323.52],["for",323.6,323.72],["instance,",323.72,324.0],["long",324.68,324.88],["-established",324.88,325.56],["forests",325.56,326.06],["usually",326.06,326.68],["support",326.68,327.0],["more",327.0,327.32],["species",327.32,327.8],["than",327.8,328.34]]},{"start":328.34,"end":334.14,"text":"newer plantations of trees, and old, natural meadowland is much better than land which","words":[["newer",328.34,328.72],["plantations",328.72,329.42],["of",329.42,329.6],["trees,",329.6,329.9],["and",330.54,330.76],["old,",330.76,331.12],["natural",331.22,331.68],["meadowland",331.68,332.32],["is",332.32,332.84],["much",332.84,333.1],["better",333.1,333.44],["than",333.44,333.64],["land",333.64,333.96],["which",333.96,334.14]]},{"start":334.14,"end":339.52,"text":"has recently been farmed. And there is a small number of highly-specialised species that","words":[["has",334.14,334.28],["recently",334.28,334.68],["been",334.68,334.96],["farmed.",334.96,335.48],["And",335.86,336.42],["there",336.42,336.56],["is",336.56,336.68],["a",336.68,336.82],["small",336.82,337.0],["number",337.0,337.34],["of",337.34,337.52],["highly",337.52,337.8],["-specialised",337.8,338.56],["species",338.56,338.88],["that",338.88,339.52]]},{"start":339.52,"end":345.82,"text":"live in unusual habitats. For instance, the blind snail spends its whole life buried","words":[["live",339.52,339.74],["in",339.74,339.96],["unusual",339.96,340.58],["habitats.",340.58,341.3],["For",341.98,342.18],["instance,",342.18,342.42],["the",343.02,343.2],["blind",343.2,343.6],["snail",343.6,344.04],["spends",344.04,344.64],["its",344.64,344.88],["whole",344.88,345.12],["life",345.12,345.4],["buried",345.4,345.82]]},{"start":345.82,"end":351.68,"text":"under the ground. It's been reported living at depths of two metres, and particularly","words":[["under",345.82,346.22],["the",346.22,346.42],["ground.",346.42,346.8],["It's",347.58,347.86],["been",347.86,348.04],["reported",348.04,348.48],["living",348.48,348.8],["at",348.8,349.0],["depths",349.0,349.26],["of",349.26,349.46],["two",349.46,349.88],["metres,",349.88,350.36],["and",350.94,351.18],["particularly",351.18,351.68]]},{"start":351.68,"end":357.46,"text":"likes the cavities in old, buried bones apparently. But species like these are exceptional.","words":[["likes",351.68,352.02],["the",352.02,352.2],["cavities",352.2,352.62],["in",352.62,352.88],["old,",352.88,353.24],["buried",353.4,353.66],["bones",353.66,354.12],["apparently.",354.12,354.62],["But",355.38,355.62],["species",355.62,355.92],["like",355.92,356.26],["these",356.26,356.48],["are",356.48,356.86],["exceptional.",356.86,357.46]]},{"start":358.68,"end":364.4,"text":"But wherever they live, gastropods are often sensitive to pollution, and they don't thrive","words":[["But",358.68,359.12],["wherever",359.12,359.44],["they",359.44,359.72],["live,",359.72,360.02],["gastropods",360.52,361.1],["are",361.1,361.28],["often",361.28,361.56],["sensitive",361.56,362.08],["to",362.08,362.36],["pollution,",362.36,362.8],["and",363.34,363.72],["they",363.72,363.86],["don't",363.86,364.08],["thrive",364.08,364.4]]},{"start":364.4,"end":369.96,"text":"in areas contaminated by agrochemicals. This means that they are a reliable indication","words":[["in",364.4,364.6],["areas",364.6,364.92],["contaminated",364.92,365.5],["by",365.5,365.98],["agrochemicals.",365.98,367.06],["This",367.72,368.08],["means",368.08,368.4],["that",368.4,368.62],["they",368.62,368.76],["are",368.76,368.92],["a",368.92,369.02],["reliable",369.02,369.32],["indication",369.32,369.96]]},{"start":369.96,"end":372.16,"text":"of how healthy our environment is.","words":[["of",369.96,370.36],["how",370.36,370.54],["healthy",370.54,371.0],["our",371.0,371.32],["environment",371.32,371.74],["is.",371.74,372.16]]},{"start":373.0,"end":376.42,"text":"Now, at this point, I'd like to consider Habitat and Management.","words":[["Now,",373.0,373.3],["at",373.66,373.86],["this",373.86,374.04],["point,",374.04,374.3],["I'd",374.44,374.6],["like",374.6,374.7],["to",374.7,374.84],["consider",374.84,375.24],["Habitat",375.24,375.84],["and",375.84,376.06],["Management.",376.06,376.42]]},{"start":379.96,"end":382.06,"text":"That is the end of part four.","words":[["That",379.96,380.6],["is",380.6,380.74],["the",380.74,380.88],["end",380.88,381.22],["of",381.22,381.4],["part",381.4,381.62],["four.",381.62,382.06]]},{"start":382.8,"end":386.36,"text":"You now have one minute to check your answers to part four.","words":[["You",382.8,383.0],["now",383.0,383.26],["have",383.26,383.62],["one",383.62,383.92],["minute",383.92,384.36],["to",384.36,384.66],["check",384.66,384.96],["your",384.96,385.16],["answers",385.16,385.56],["to",385.56,385.8],["part",385.8,386.0],["four.",386.0,386.36]]},{"start":446.37,"end":448.45,"text":"That is the end of the listening test.","words":[["That",446.37,446.83],["is",446.83,446.99],["the",446.99,447.15],["end",447.15,447.51],["of",447.51,447.69],["the",447.69,447.81],["listening",447.81,448.07],["test.",448.07,448.45]]},{"start":449.19,"end":454.17,"text":"You now have ten minutes to transfer your answers to the listening answer sheet.","words":[["You",449.19,449.41],["now",449.41,449.67],["have",449.67,450.05],["ten",450.05,450.37],["minutes",450.37,450.77],["to",450.77,451.13],["transfer",451.13,451.65],["your",451.65,451.91],["answers",451.91,452.33],["to",452.33,452.83],["the",452.83,452.99],["listening",452.99,453.31],["answer",453.31,453.79],["sheet.",453.79,454.17]]},{"start":935.0,"end":936.34,"text":"You have two minutes left.","words":[["You",935.0,935.34],["have",935.34,935.52],["two",935.52,935.74],["minutes",935.74,936.02],["left.",936.02,936.34]]},{"start":996.59,"end":997.81,"text":"You have one minute 